<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lancashire</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lancashire is a county in north-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> that became the centre of the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> textile industry during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/industrial-revolution">Industrial Revolution</a>. Its mills processed raw cotton imported from overseas and exported finished cloth across the world, including to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. The industry tied Lancashire closely to the trade networks of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lancashire.jpg" alt="Lancashire" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Peter McDermott · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Clitheroe_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4067941.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
